                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Quick Review: A relatively weak and uninspiring Endless Runner that gets boring as soon as the joke wears off (which is quick). At £4.79 or your regional equvilent this is an expensive game for the genre.\n\nLonger-ish Review: \"Where's My Mommy?\" is an endless runner that sees you mother get ejected out of your hosts poop hole and into the great beyond. Enter our protagonist a considerably small piece of fecal matter who must go on an endless runner quest to find her. \n\nThe game has 3 main mechanics; the ability to jump over obstacles, the ability to go squishy to pass through gaps & permeable onstacles and the ability to go hard and break stuff like condoms. \n\nWhile this all sounds like a silly fun laugh that is pretty much it. you amble through the levels basically trying to work out (and sometimes guess) which objects require you to go hard and which squishy. It is bizarre logic most of the time which is which and totally random others. Either way this mechanic definitely did not add to the game and I felt it would have worked much better just giving me things to jump over and dodge.\n\nFor fans of the genre there could be a fun 5 minutes here but for the price there really is better examples of the genre on the market.\n\nFor our initial first play of the game check our our video below: http://www.thegametutor.co.uk/videos/literal-first-play/160302_wheres-my-mommy-literal-first-play\n\nA KEY FOR THE GAME WAS KINDLY PROVIDED BY THE DEVELOPER FOR REVIEW PURPOSES. MY THOUGHTS AND OPINIONS ARE MY OWN.\n\nIf you have enjoyed this review and found it informative please join our Curator group to get more recommendations http://steamcommunity.com/groups/gametutor#curation",
